</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 2:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In the Otero letter BTK said something to the effect: <BR> <BR>&#34;Since sexual deviantes don&#39;t or can&#39;t change their MO, I won&#39;t change mine dum dum dum...bind, torture, kill&#34; <BR> <BR>This suggests 1&#41;He realizes that he has the option to change his MO if he decides to. 2&#41;as far as he&#39;s concerned, to maintain his MO, he only has to bind, torture and kill.  <BR> <BR>So he leaves himself a lot of options...and it&#39;s BTK, so he can&#39;t be trusted anyway.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
