<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8515"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Km<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Km<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 10:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Some of the reasons why I think the Davis murder is a BTK job is because her driver&#39;s license was taken, her camera was taken, jewelry was taken, someone ate a bowl of cereal and left it in the sink, and the object that was used to throw to gain access to her house.  In BTK&#39;s Communication 8, he used a cereal box and a brick.  Until last night&#39;s interview with Jeff Davis, the object used to gain access to her house was always referred to as a brick.  This same communication was found in close proximity to her house.  I am also curious to know if Communication 7 referred to the Marine Hedge murder since it was also in the same area.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
