<!--Post: 9006--><!--Time: 1109383440-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9006"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 6:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->How about 4 houses down from Marine Hedges? Gee guys, what do you think? I know why we never heard a scream or a struggle across the street, or a car pull up etc. Becuase he walked to her house. Piece of %&amp;&#42;$!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9006-->
<!--Post: 9229--><!--Time: 1109438926-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9229"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 9:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Delores Davis, your murderer has been brought to justice ... may you rest in peace <IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/happy.gif" ALT=":-&#41;" BORDER=0><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9229-->
<!--Post: 9263--><!--Time: 1109453872-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9263"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Freya<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Freya<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 1:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Amen<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9263-->
<!--Post: 9298--><!--Time: 1109465088-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9298"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Neverstop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Neverstop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 4:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Funny how a murderer can, himself, get investigative theory wrong. And obviously his &#34;degree in criminology&#34; didn&#39;t help him any. According to Robert Keppel, in his book on signatures which killers leave, it&#39;s the signature, not the M.O. that doesn&#39;t change, Mr. BTK. That&#39;s because part of what constitutes a signature is the part of the act that provides satisfaction to the killer. So of course it is then by definition something he simply can&#39;t leave out, or else why kill at all? As in, why play golf at all or why have sex at all or why eat dessert at all? It has to DO something for you or it&#39;s useless. But the M.O can change a lot because it&#39;s nothing more than a means to an end. And a bright relentless guy WILL change what he has to to keep on having his KAKE and eating it too. By the way, was D.R. working as a dog catcher and a zoning dude for Sedgewick County, and would he have been personally acquainted with the oft-quoted Sedgewick Co. Sheriff and other county personnel? Thanks for your responses.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9298-->
<!--Post: 9976--><!--Time: 1109715457-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9976"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 2:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey - CNN.COm has a pic of a piece of jewelry...maybe it is how they linked DTDC to Dee Davis...I have never seen this piece of jewelry before....go look.. <BR>cnn.com you will see our boy under &#34;developing story&#34;  click on &#34;timeline&#34;  pic is with Feb 2005. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9976-->
<!--Post: 10615--><!--Time: 1110060026-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10615"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 05, 2005 - 2:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->More evidence:  She had FootPrints near her <BR> <BR>Since Tom hasn&#39;t made a separate file for delores or marine yet, I&#39;ll post this here:   <BR> <BR>&#34;A teenager walking his dog discovered the bloated body of a woman under a bridge in northwest Sedgwick County on Friday morning. <BR> <BR>Sedgwick County sheriff&#39;s Capt. James Elvins said the identity of the woman had not been determined. The 15-year-old boy found the body after chasing his dog under a bridge at 117th North and 3500 West. He went to his home and called 911. <BR>         <BR>Investigators Friday were taking casts of footprints and tire marks found near the body. An investigator in a helicopter took aerial photographs.&#34; <BR> <BR>Apparently they had linked Delores case to Marine&#39;s the day they identified her ... or at least they tried to link them according to an early ninties report.  The mask found was a &#34;female&#34; mask, and what was taken from her was &#34;costume jewlery&#34;  <BR> <BR>Davis&#39; son has always though the two were linked, but did not get his profile right: <BR> <BR>&#34;Based on the legwork, Davis compiled a psychological profile of the killer and pieced together a step-by-step scenario of how the murder appears to have occurred. <BR> <BR>He said the killer is a white male, 25 to 35 years old, 6 feet tall,  <BR>180 to 190 pounds; &#34;functionally psychopathic obsessive-compulsive &#40;behavior&#41;, analytical, intelligent, socially withdrawn, has repressed rage against authority figures, and is possibly a latent homosexual or transsexual who was abused, neglected or ignored as a child by a significant female figure.&#34; <BR> <BR> <BR>In 1991, an Eastborough death of a woman had similar connection to Delores Davis and Marine Hedge and a connection was suggested at that time: <BR> <BR>&#34;Donna Jabara Baker bled to death after being stabbed repeatedly in the chest, autopsy results showed Wednesday. <BR> <BR>The body of the 55-year-old woman was discovered Tuesday when emergency crews responded to a report of a fire in her Eastborough home. A relative who had come by to see the woman found smoke coming from a pile of clothes at about 5:30 p.m. and called 911. <BR>         <BR>Sedgwick County sheriff&#39;s Capt. Jim Elvins said the death was the first homicide in the history of Eastborough. The city was incorporated in 1937.&#34; <BR> <BR>Wether or not this case was solved, I&#39;m not sure.  However another connection comes in fact that the house was burned.  A circumstantial connection could be made with Barbara Smith and Carol Mould where attempted burning of the houses also happened. <BR> <BR>At this time Isabel Moore&#39;s murder happened and many were trying to tie all these cases together.  This would not happen.  Davis and Hedge would be linked to the BTK this year, and Moore&#39;s death was balmed on the killer James Cromwell.  &#40;A new post was made on his murders in teh Theories section&#41; <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10615-->
<!--Post: 10617--><!--Time: 1110061764-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10617"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 05, 2005 - 2:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Alan Wayne Kingsley was convicted of the murder of Donna Jabara Baker.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10617-->
